---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import { site } from '../../content/site'
import portrait from '../../assets/photos/ryan-amarit.webp'
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Ryan Amarit is a web lead and product engineer with nine years of building websites, design systems and products."
  palette="about"
>
  <section class="wrap page-hero" data-section="about" data-gl="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="page-title" data-split>Strategy to shipped code.</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:2rem">{site.intro}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap about-grid" data-section="about-body">
    <div class="portrait">
      <Image
        src={portrait}
        alt="Ryan Amarit"
        width={1280}
        widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280]}
        sizes="(min-width: 900px) 42vw, 100vw"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="prose-lg">
      <p>
        I lead the marketing web team at 8am (formerly AffiniPay). We're a private equity–backed legal
        tech company with a handful of B2B SaaS brands, including MyCase, LawPay, CASEpeer and
        Docketwise.
      </p>

      <dl class="facts">
        {site.facts.map((fact) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{fact.label}</dt>
            <dd>{fact.value}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>

      <p>
        Most of our marketing leads come through the websites, so the work matters well beyond how a
        page looks. I set the technical direction, moved eight brand sites onto one Astro codebase and a
        shared design system, and help run the A/B tests that decide what ships. New pages now go live
        40% faster.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm hands-on, and I still write code. I also work with Marketing, Growth, Design, Brand and
        Content, manage our agency partners, and mentor the developer on my team. And I care a lot about
        how it all feels for the person on the other side of the screen.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm really into how AI is changing the way small teams work. At 8am I brought in AI code reviews
        that push back on every change, a pipeline that turns bug reports into pull requests, and
        spec-driven development. On the side I'm building RulerIQ, which shows brands what AI assistants
        say about them, with AI coding agents working from specs I write and review.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before 8am I spent three years at Balcom Agency running discovery, building client sites and
        training client teams, and before that I helped Fluke automate a big migration to Drupal. Along
        the way, sites I've led or built have picked up an Awwwards Honorable Mention, a CSSDA Special
        Kudos and a Best of Interactive at the Fort Worth American Advertising Awards.
      </p>

      <p style="margin-top:2.5rem">
        <a class="btn btn-accent" href="/projects/">See the work <span class="btn-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
